---
import SectionHeader from './SectionHeader.astro';
import ProjectCard from './ProjectCard.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<section
  id="academic"
  data-accent="59 130 246"
  class="py-24 px-6 max-w-6xl mx-auto"
>
  <SectionHeader
    index="01"
    title="Academic & Mathematical Work"
    subtitle="Simulations have really helped me understand some mathematical enviroments. When aproaching a problem or a new subject I look for ways to simulate it so I can better understand it and interact with it in real time. Below are some of the sims I've built for this purpose."
  />

  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">

    <!-- Wide card: paper + simulation together -->
    <article class="reveal group relative border border-white/[0.08] rounded-sm transition-all duration-300 overflow-hidden md:col-span-2 hover:border-[color:rgb(var(--accent)/0.35)] hover:bg-[color:rgb(var(--accent)/0.05)]">

      <!-- Three screenshots in a row -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-3 border-b border-white/[0.06]">
        <img src={`${base}cr3bp1.png`} alt="CR3BP trajectory over effective potential" class="w-full aspect-video object-cover opacity-75 group-hover:opacity-95 transition-opacity duration-300 border-r border-white/[0.06]" loading="lazy" />
        <img src={`${base}cr3bp2.png`} alt="CR3BP Hill surfaces and Lagrange points" class="w-full aspect-video object-cover opacity-75 group-hover:opacity-95 transition-opacity duration-300 border-r border-white/[0.06]" loading="lazy" />
        <img src={`${base}cr3bp3.png`} alt="CR3BP Lagrange point diamond configuration" class="w-full aspect-video object-cover opacity-75 group-hover:opacity-95 transition-opacity duration-300" loading="lazy" />
      </div>

      <div class="p-6">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3">
          <h3 class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border border-[color:rgb(var(--accent)/0.6)] bg-[color:rgb(var(--accent)/0.08)] text-white/85 group-hover:text-white group-hover:border-[color:rgb(var(--accent)/0.9)] group-hover:bg-[color:rgb(var(--accent)/0.15)] transition-colors">
            Celestial Mechanics — Circular Restricted 3-Body Problem
          </h3>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 shrink-0">
            <a href={`${base}celestial-mechanics.pdf`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-xs tracking-widest px-3 py-1.5 rounded-sm border border-[color:rgb(var(--accent)/0.7)] bg-[color:rgb(var(--accent)/0.12)] text-white hover:bg-[color:rgb(var(--accent)/0.25)] hover:border-[color:rgb(var(--accent))] active:scale-95 transition-all duration-150 shrink-0">Read Paper ↗</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-white/45 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Real-time sim of the Circular Restricted Three-Body Problem, the gravitational dynamics of a massless particle like a satellite under two massive bodies in circular orbit. Numerical integrator for the trajectories with a trail renderer, rendered on the background the energy level of each point of the screen as a color-mapped landscape, computed all five Lagrange equilibrium points (L1–L5), and visualized Hill surfaces as forbidden-region boundaries. Accompanied by a formal paper.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          {["Numerical Integration", "Celestial Mechanics", "Scientific Visualization", "C#", "Unity"].map(t => (
            <span class="font-mono text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded-sm bg-white/[0.05] text-white/35 border border-white/[0.08]">{t}</span>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Simulation clips below -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 border-t border-white/[0.06]">
        <video src={`${base}cr3bp-sim1.mp4`} poster={`${base}cr3bp-sim1-poster.jpg`} data-poster={`${base}cr3bp-sim1-poster.jpg`} loop muted playsinline preload="metadata" class="w-full aspect-video object-cover opacity-70 group-hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity duration-300 border-r border-white/[0.06]"></video>
        <video src={`${base}cr3bp-sim3.mp4`} poster={`${base}cr3bp-sim3-poster.jpg`} data-poster={`${base}cr3bp-sim3-poster.jpg`} loop muted playsinline preload="metadata" class="w-full aspect-video object-cover opacity-70 group-hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity duration-300"></video>
      </div>

      <div class="absolute left-0 top-4 bottom-4 w-px bg-[color:rgb(var(--accent))] opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-50 transition-opacity duration-300 rounded-full"></div>
    </article>

    <ProjectCard
      title="Power Iteration — Eigenvalue Visualizer"
      video={`${base}power-iteration.mp4`}
      description="Real-time visualization of the power iteration algorithm. A point cloud of vectors fills 3D space — on each step, the linear transformation is applied to every point simultaneously. The cloud converges geometrically toward the dominant eigenvector direction, making the abstract convergence rate visible as a physical collapse in space."
      tags={["Scientific Visualization", "Linear Algebra", "Numerical Methods", "Point Cloud", "C#"]}
    />
    <ProjectCard
      image={`${base}isoperimetric.jpg`}
      title="Desigualdad Isoperimétrica"
      description="A proof of the isoperimetric inequality ℓ² ≥ 4πA — that among all closed simple curves with a given perimeter, the circle encloses maximum area. The proof reparametrizes the curve by arc length, expresses both ℓ² and A in terms of Fourier coefficients, then uses the Parseval identity to reduce the inequality to a purely algebraic statement. Equality holds only for the circle."
      tags={["Analysis", "Fourier Series", "Differential Geometry", "Proof"]}
      links={[{ label: "Read Paper", href: `${base}isoperimetrica.pdf` }]}
    />

  </div>
</section>
